Pulse 5 is the optimal "merge window". Without nested timing, the closest pulse is 13.8 MeV below barrier.

Experimental Proposal
Required: Fe ion beam, Pb target, 2 tunable gamma sources 10-50 MeV, 1 high-energy gamma 100-200 MeV.  
Prediction: Detection of $^{264}\text{X}_{108}$ alpha decay only when Pulse 5 timing at 194.0 MeV with 5 half-pulses is used.

Conclusion
Dual-Fibonacci timing transforms fusion from stochastic collision to deterministic conduction. This provides a low-cost pathway to test heavy element synthesis and radiation-resistant materials for interstellar applications.  

